First, we start with the total number of guests that the hotel was fully booked with before any extra fans arrived. That's 100. We will start from here and work our way through the different events that went on that day until we get to the answer. 
The first event is that 24 guests opt for an early checkout. We subtract 24 from 100: \begin{align*}
100-24=76
\end{align*} The reasoning behind this step is to get the total number of guests that are left at the hotel after the early check outs.
Then, we are told that 15 guests opt for a late checkout. Since at this point, there are 76 guests left at the hotel, 15 more will make the hotel have its full capacity. Therefore, we have
\begin{align*}
76+15=91
\end{align*} Now, we are told that in the afternoon twice as many people checked in as those who opted for a late checkout. Twice as many people would be $2\times 15=30$. So,
\begin{align*}
91+30=121
\end{align*} We add those 30 people who have checked in in the afternoon to the 91 people who still have the hotel's full capacity.
Lastly, we are told that 7 more people checked in after midday. Since there are currently 121 guests already in the hotel, the number of guests that the hotel would have after 7 more guests show up would be
\begin{align*}
121+7=\boxed{128}
\end{align*} Hence, the hotel would have \begin{align*}\boxed{128}\ end{align*} guests.

